message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "The Jailbreak Robustness Ladder: Separating Safety Failure from Comprehension Failure in Cross-Lingual Attacks on Open Language Models"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nuhan
    given-names: Arian
    email: ariannuhan41@gmail.com
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-29
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Nuharian/jailbreak-robustness-ladder"
keywords:
  - AI safety
  - jailbreak
  - cross-lingual
  - multilingual NLP
  - LLM evaluation
  - low-resource languages
abstract: >-
  An open, API-key-free harness that measures how prompt transformations, including translation
  into seven languages, degrade the refusal behaviour of open language models, and separates
  genuine safety failure from comprehension failure with a three-way judge and a
  comprehension-controlled attack-success rate.
